Soju: winemac shows Metal drawing of a window whose top-level window another process owns.
Chromium's GPU process (the EA app, Rockstar Games Launcher, Ubisoft Connect) draws with DXMT or
D3DMetal into a window of the browser process; the driver had no view for it there and the
launcher stayed white or black. The drawing process now renders into a CAMetalLayer it exports
through a CAContext, and the owner of the top-level window shows it with a CALayerHost placed on
the window's client area, kept in place as either side moves, resizes, shows or hides it, and
removed when the drawing ends or the window is destroyed.

